{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7fapqln7zopy5jeaiqtrptzvur4hzoubic3j3usu65t2ngem2rxa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What the library is\n\nThe entire C library is one 48-line file exporting one function: `void hsl_to_rgb(float *dest, const float *src)`. No `[features]` in `Cargo.toml`, no `option()`/`#ifdef` in the C build → **exactly one feature combination** (`{}`).\n\n## Artifacts created (crate root)\n\n| file | contents |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` inventory; C source completeness audit; symbol diff = **empty** |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 21-row error-surface table + the mechanical grep transcript it was derived from |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 34-row configuration-surface table (H × S × L × pointer-relationship) |\n| `verify.sh` | extracts `[features]`, builds the power set, runs check/build/symbol-diff/test per combo |\n| `tests/common/mod.rs` | harness: dlopens both `.so`s, guard-word buffers, SplitMix64 PRNG |\n| `tests/differential.rs` | 37 tests — CONFIGS rows 1–34 + symbol parity |\n| `tests/errors.rs` | 23 tests — ERRORS rows 1–21 + FFI-boundary sweep |\n\n**60/60 tests pass.** Every call goes through `dlopen`/`dlsym` on both shared objects — the Rust crate is never linked into the test binary — and every comparison is on raw `u32` bit patterns, so `±0.0` and NaN sign/payload differences fail.\n\n## Three real bugs found and fixed in the Rust\n\n1. **`fmodf` bound to the wrong implementation.** Rust's `%` on `f32` was satisfied by `compiler_builtins`' *statically linked* `fmodf`, not glibc's. `h = -inf` reaches `fmodf(-inf, 2.0f)` **and uses the result** (the negative-hue branch), so the NaN bit pattern was observable. Now `#[link(name = \"m\")] extern \"C\" { fmodf }` — the Rust `.so` imports the identical `fmodf@GLIBC_2.2.5`, asserted by a test.\n2. **`read_unaligned`/`write_unaligned` diverged on null pointers.** Their debug-only `assert_unsafe_precondition!` turned the C's `SIGSEGV` into a panic-abort. Reverted to plain `*ptr` derefs, the literal analogue of `src[0]`.\n3. **Debug-profile UB instrumentation.** The C reference is `-O0` with no instrumentation; Rust's `dev` profile injects alignment checks that abort where the C's `movss` just works. The harness builds the unoptimized variant with `-Cdebug-assertions=off` so it is an apples-to-apples counterpart. Both Rust builds now match C on null pointers (all three `SIGSEGV`) and on mis-aligned buffers.\n\n## C quirks confirmed replicated\n\nThe third guard is `h < 120.0f && h < 180.0f`, not `h >= 120.0f`. Tests pin down both consequences: hues in `[120,180)` fall to the final `else` (that sector is dead code), and **negative** hues silently execute the sector-3 body. `-0.0` saturation takes the early-out; `-0.0` hue does not count as negative.\n\n## Test-suite validation\n\nRather than trust green checkmarks, I mutation-tested: 5 of 7 behaviour-changing mutations were **killed** (both float operand-order swaps that matter, the \"bug fix\", an `addss` operand swap, dropping the `-0.0` early-out). The 2 survivors are provably equivalent (`c*0.5 ≡ 0.5*c` and `l+l ≡ 2.0*l` are bit-exact for all 2³² `f32`, NaN quieting included), so they are not coverage gaps.\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was modified apart from the `build/` directory the task's own cmake command creates."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":663,"cache_read_input_tokens":143135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":663,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e184715-bcf6-4ef2-94b0-032cbc18aa4f","uuid":"06c0ca3a-ff55-4ec7-8c85-94dfa2a81646","timestamp":"2026-08-19T12:47:12.240Z"}
